m-dj98"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm-cli 2026.9.3; Node 26.5.0; Linux; fresh merge-driver install"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Create one item, diverge two branches, update the same scalar at different timestamps, then merge in both directions with default, --prefer ours, and --prefer theirs; observe the same lexicographically smaller value retained."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A documented deterministic policy preserves direction-independent convergence while choosing by meaningful recorded evidence, and any advertised preference control either affects its declared class or explicitly excludes it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"stable_value_order retains lexicographically smaller statuses and numeric values independent of write time, merge direction, and --prefer."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk/merge"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-dlx7v7","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-09-03T18:06:36.495Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-qckpnq","kind":"recurs_from","created_at":"2026-09-03T18:06:36.495Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-03T18:06:36.495Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1184. All-status duplicate check searched scalar merge, stable value order, preference, recency, and direction lineages; pm-qckpnq closed the truthful requested_preference receipt field and pm-dlx7v7 closed direction independence, but neither makes the winning scalar policy recency-aware. This is new recurrence/semantic-policy w